  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Persistence At All",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "RAM Is The Only Copy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Authoritative dataset lives in RAM, not on disk",
            "Process exit loses everything not yet written out",
            "Persistence = write state so a restart can rebuild it",
            "Redis ACKs the write before it hits the platter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Failure Classes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Failure",
            "What dies",
            "Survives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Process crash",
              "`redis-server`",
              "page cache"
            ],
            [
              "OS / host crash",
              "page cache",
              "fsynced bytes"
            ],
            [
              "Disk failure",
              "the files",
              "offsite copy"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Durability, RPO, RTO"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Durability: an ACKed write survives a named failure class",
            "RPO: data you accept losing, in time (e.g. 1s)",
            "RTO: how long a restart takes to become serving-ready",
            "Each policy guards a different class — say which"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Mechanisms"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tree",
          "spec": {
            "root": "Redis persistence",
            "branches": [
              {
                "label": "RDB",
                "children": [
                  "periodic snapshot",
                  "binary dump"
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "AOF",
                "children": [
                  "command log",
                  "fsync dial"
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "Both",
                "children": [
                  "they run together"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Not The Same As Replication",
          "text": "A replica protects against host loss; persistence protects against restart amnesia. Production wants both."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Replicas Copy Bugs Too",
          "items": [
            "A stray `FLUSHALL` replicates instantly",
            "An hour-old `dump.rdb` still holds the data",
            "Backups beat replicas for human error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading The State"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "redis-cli INFO persistence",
            "# rdb_*  aof_*  loading",
            "# rdb_last_bgsave_status, aof_last_write_status",
            "# one command, every state in this handbook"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Zero Persistence Is Legit",
          "items": [
            "`save \"\"` plus `appendonly no`",
            "Cache-only nodes are rebuildable by design",
            "Only when a real system of record sits behind"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick By Need",
          "text": "RDB for backups and fast restarts, AOF for a low RPO, both for production."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "\"We run an AOF, so we're durable\" — true?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "False until you also state `appendfsync`",
            "`appendfsync no` can lose ~30s on a host crash",
            "A durability claim needs a policy plus a failure class"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "RDB Snapshots: What & How",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What An RDB Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compact binary dump of the whole keyspace",
            "Point-in-time: one instant, one file",
            "Default `dump.rdb`, written inside `dir`",
            "Versioned, self-describing, CRC64 trailer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "dbfilename dump.rdb   # names the file",
            "dir /var/lib/redis    # Redis chdir()s here",
            "rdbcompression yes    # LZF strings, cheap CPU",
            "rdbchecksum yes       # CRC64, independent knob"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SAVE vs BGSAVE"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "`SAVE`",
              "items": [
                "Main thread",
                "Blocks every client",
                "Scripts, shutdown only"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "`BGSAVE`",
              "items": [
                "Forks a child",
                "Parent keeps serving",
                "The normal path"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Automatic Triggers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "save 900 1       # 1 change in 15 min",
            "save 300 10      # 10 changes in 5 min",
            "save 60 10000    # 10k changes in 1 min",
            "save \"\"          # disables all of them"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`CONFIG SET save \"\"` does it at runtime",
            "Implicit BGSAVE on `SHUTDOWN` if saves configured",
            "Also on `DEBUG RELOAD` and full replica sync"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Atomic On Disk"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "fork child",
              "write temp file",
              "checksum",
              "rename() over dump.rdb"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never A Half File",
          "text": "Readers see the old snapshot or the new one. `rename()` is atomic, so a backup copy needs no locking."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Watching A Save Land"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "redis-cli LASTSAVE     # unix ts of last success",
            "redis-cli INFO persistence",
            "# rdb_bgsave_in_progress, rdb_last_save_time",
            "# rdb_last_bgsave_status, rdb_changes_since_last_save"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Backup Recipe",
          "items": [
            "Poll `LASTSAVE` until it advances",
            "`redis-check-rdb dump.rdb` before trusting it",
            "`cp dump.rdb snap-2026-09-07.rdb`",
            "One immutable file — ship it anywhere"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Fork, Copy-on-Write & Snapshot Cost",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What fork() Actually Does",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Child gets a logical copy of parent memory",
            "Pages are shared and marked read-only",
            "No data bytes copied — only page tables"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Copy-On-Write Tax"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "memory-cells",
          "spec": {
            "label": "shared pages after fork",
            "cells": [
              "r/o",
              "r/o",
              "WRITE",
              "copied 4KB",
              "r/o",
              "r/o"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parent mutates a shared page: kernel copies 4KB",
            "Memory grows with write rate, not dataset size",
            "Worst case a BGSAVE doubles RSS — keep headroom",
            "`rdb_last_cow_size` = bytes copied last BGSAVE"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Fork Stall"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Dataset",
            "Page table copy",
            "Felt as"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1 GB",
              "~10-20 ms",
              "latency spike"
            ],
            [
              "8 GB",
              "~80-160 ms",
              "p99 blowup"
            ],
            [
              "THP on",
              "2 MB per copy",
              "hundreds of ms"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stall scales with dataset size, not write rate",
            "`INFO stats` `latest_fork_usec` = exact last stall",
            "Alert on it — that number is your fork budget"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Host Prep, Two Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "echo never > /sys/kernel/mm/transparent_hugepage/enabled",
            "sysctl -w vm.overcommit_memory=1",
            "# THP off: COW copies 4KB pages, not 2MB",
            "# overcommit 1: fork() survives RSS+COW > RAM"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Redis Warns You At Boot",
          "text": "The THP warning in the log is not cosmetic. Leaving it on is the classic source of mystery spikes during saves."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "When Fork Fails",
          "items": [
            "`rdb_last_bgsave_status:err` appears",
            "`stop-writes-on-bgsave-error yes` then rejects writes",
            "Client sees `MISCONF`, not silent loss"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Child At A Time"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "BGSAVE, AOF rewrite and disk replica sync all fork",
            "Same COW tax applies to all three",
            "A BGSAVE asked for during a rewrite is deferred",
            "Watch `rdb_bgsave_scheduled:1`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Lowering The Bill",
          "items": [
            "Shard into smaller instances",
            "Fewer `save` points",
            "Run snapshots on a replica, not the primary",
            "Keep `maxmemory` well under RAM"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "AOF: The Append-Only Log",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Log Of Mutations",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every write command appended in RESP wire format",
            "Logged after execution — only successful mutations",
            "Append-only: no seeks, no in-place edits",
            "So a truncated tail is the only realistic corruption"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "appendonly yes",
            "appendfilename \"appendonly.aof\"",
            "appenddirname \"appendonlydir\"   # Redis 7+"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Commands Get Normalised"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "You ran",
            "AOF stores",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`SPOP s`",
              "`SREM s m`",
              "random pick"
            ],
            [
              "`EXPIRE k 60`",
              "`PEXPIREAT k <ms>`",
              "absolute time"
            ],
            [
              "`INCRBYFLOAT k .1`",
              "`SET k <result>`",
              "float drift"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Replay Must Be Deterministic",
          "text": "Rewriting non-deterministic commands before logging is what makes a replay land on the exact same dataset."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Writes Per Command"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "command",
              "AOF buffer",
              "write() page cache",
              "fsync() platter"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Buffer flushes once per event-loop pass (`beforeSleep`)",
            "Not once per command — the batching is deliberate",
            "`write()` and `fsync()` are separate steps",
            "That split is the whole durability story"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recovery Is A Replay"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Redis starts a fake client on boot",
            "Feeds the log back command by command",
            "`aof-load-truncated yes` (default) tolerates a cut tail",
            "It warns and keeps appending instead of refusing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keeping It From Growing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "auto-aof-rewrite-percentage 100  # doubled since base",
            "auto-aof-rewrite-min-size 64mb   # and past this floor",
            "# manual kick: redis-cli BGREWRITEAOF"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "INFO Keys To Know",
          "items": [
            "`aof_enabled`, `aof_rewrite_in_progress`",
            "`aof_last_bgrewrite_status`, `aof_last_write_status`",
            "`aof_current_size` vs `aof_base_size`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Safe to switch AOF on in a live server?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`CONFIG SET appendonly yes` — it does not block",
            "It kicks off a background rewrite to build the base",
            "`redis-check-aof --fix` truncates a bad trailing command"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "fsync Policies: The Durability Dial",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Exactly Three Settings",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "`appendfsync`",
            "Loss window",
            "Throughput"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`always`",
              "~1 command",
              "<10k ops/s"
            ],
            [
              "`everysec`",
              "~1-2 s",
              "near full"
            ],
            [
              "`no`",
              "~30 s",
              "fastest"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`everysec` is the default and the sane one",
            "`always` fsyncs before replying to the client",
            "`no` leaves it to kernel dirty-page writeback"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Distinction That Matters"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "`write()` saves you from",
              "items": [
                "redis-server crash",
                "`kill -9`",
                "OOM killer"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "`fsync()` saves you from",
              "items": [
                "kernel panic",
                "power cut",
                "host loss"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Process Kill Is Cheap",
          "text": "Even `appendfsync no` loses nothing when only redis-server dies — the kernel still owns the buffer."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "everysec Is Really 2s"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A background thread fsyncs once a second",
            "If that thread is still busy, the main thread waits",
            "Documented delay of up to another second",
            "Budget 2s of loss, not 1s"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rewrites Fight The Disk"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "no-appendfsync-on-rewrite yes",
            "# main AOF fsync paused while a child writes",
            "# = appendfsync no for the whole rewrite window",
            "# buys latency, sells durability. Know it first."
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hardware Tells Lies",
          "items": [
            "fsync hits the platter only if write cache is off",
            "...or battery / capacitor backed",
            "Consumer SSDs report success early",
            "EBS and PD fsync sits in the low milliseconds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Per-Write Durability"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "SET order:9 paid",
            "WAITAOF 1 1 100   # 1 local fsync, 1 replica, 100ms",
            "WAIT 1 100        # replication only, NOT fsync",
            "# 7.2+; confusing the two is a real outage"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "One Node Is Never Enough",
          "text": "`always` on a single box still dies with the box. Cross-machine durability needs a replica plus `WAITAOF`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "AOF Rewrite & Multi-Part AOF",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Log Grows Forever",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`INCR counter` a million times = a million entries",
            "...describing one integer of actual state",
            "Rewrite emits the shortest sequence that rebuilds it",
            "History discarded, current dataset kept"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "before:  INCR c   x 1,000,000",
            "after:   SET c 1000000",
            "# same dataset, one line instead of a million"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When It Fires"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "auto-aof-rewrite-percentage 100  # grown 2x aof_base_size",
            "auto-aof-rewrite-min-size 64mb   # and past the floor",
            "# 0 disables auto rewrite entirely",
            "# then the log grows until the disk fills"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`BGREWRITEAOF` forks a child that walks memory",
            "The child writes a fresh, minimal base",
            "`aof_rewrite_scheduled:1` = waiting on a running child"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Old Design vs Redis 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Pre-7",
              "items": [
                "Child writes one file",
                "Parent buffers new writes",
                "Buffer appended, then rename",
                "Memory-hungry and fiddly"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Multi-part AOF",
              "items": [
                "Child writes base only",
                "Parent appends to a new incr",
                "Manifest lists the parts",
                "No rewrite buffer at all"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Inside appendonlydir/"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "memory-cells",
          "spec": {
            "label": "appendonlydir/",
            "cells": [
              "*.manifest",
              "*.base.rdb",
              "*.1.incr.aof",
              "*.2.incr.aof"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Manifest is updated atomically at the very end",
            "Old base and incr files deleted only after that",
            "A crash mid-rewrite leaves the old manifest valid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Hybrid Format"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`aof-use-rdb-preamble yes`, default since 4.0",
            "Base is an RDB dump, not RESP commands",
            "Tail stays per-command, so durability is unchanged",
            "Loads dramatically faster than a plain AOF"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Still A Fork",
          "text": "A rewrite pays the same COW memory and `latest_fork_usec` stall as a BGSAVE — and the two never run at once."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Restart & Recovery Behaviour",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Load Precedence",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tree",
          "spec": {
            "root": "Redis boots",
            "branches": [
              {
                "label": "`appendonly yes`",
                "children": [
                  "loads AOF",
                  "ignores dump.rdb"
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "`appendonly no`",
                "children": [
                  "loads dump.rdb"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "AOF wins because it is the more complete record",
            "There is no merge — the RDB is simply not read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The #1 Loss Trap",
          "text": "Good RDB on disk, you add `appendonly yes` to the config and restart: Redis reads an empty AOF and boots an empty dataset."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# safe enablement, at runtime, RDB already loaded",
            "redis-cli CONFIG SET appendonly yes",
            "redis-cli INFO persistence | grep rewrite",
            "redis-cli CONFIG REWRITE   # persist to the file"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "While It Loads"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`INFO persistence` reports `loading:1`",
            "Clients get `-LOADING Redis is loading the dataset in memory`",
            "Progress: `loading_total_bytes`, `loading_loaded_perc`",
            "Plus `loading_eta_seconds`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "RTO By Format"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Format",
            "Load path",
            "Speed"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "RDB",
              "binary parse",
              "seconds per GB"
            ],
            [
              "Hybrid AOF",
              "RDB base + tail",
              "close behind"
            ],
            [
              "Plain AOF",
              "re-dispatch every command",
              "slowest by far"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Damaged Files"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Damage",
            "Redis does",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Bad RDB checksum",
              "refuses to start",
              "older backup"
            ],
            [
              "Truncated AOF tail",
              "loads, warns",
              "nothing"
            ],
            [
              "Corrupt AOF middle",
              "exits",
              "`redis-check-aof --fix`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--fix` cuts at the bad point — everything after is gone",
            "There is no partial RDB load, ever"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stopping Cleanly"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SHUTDOWN` does a final blocking save if saves exist",
            "`SHUTDOWN NOSAVE` skips it; `kill -9` always skips",
            "Redis 7 waits for lagging replicas, `shutdown-timeout 10`",
            "`DEBUG RELOAD` saves and reloads in place — a round-trip test"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Restore Drill",
          "items": [
            "Stop Redis first",
            "Drop the file into `dir`, right name and owner",
            "Start Redis — it loads on boot",
            "Never copy into a running instance's `dir`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "RDB vs AOF: Side by Side",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Loss, Size, Speed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "RDB",
            "AOF"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Loss window",
              "minutes",
              "~1s / ~1 cmd"
            ],
            [
              "File size",
              "compact binary",
              "much larger"
            ],
            [
              "Restart",
              "fastest",
              "slowest (plain)"
            ],
            [
              "Overhead",
              "fork spike only",
              "per-write + fsync"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hybrid AOF sits between on both size and load speed",
            "RDB costs nothing at all between snapshots",
            "AOF pays a small constant cost on every write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Operating Them"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "RDB",
            "AOF"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Backup",
              "one `cp`-able file",
              "dir + manifest"
            ],
            [
              "Point-in-time",
              "hourly restore points",
              "as of the crash"
            ],
            [
              "Disk I/O",
              "periodic burst",
              "steady append"
            ],
            [
              "Blast radius",
              "unusable wholesale",
              "truncate, salvage"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Backups Still Need RDB",
          "text": "AOF gives you \"now\". Only archived snapshots give you \"yesterday at 3pm\" — which is what a bad `FLUSHALL` needs."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Host Crash Ranking"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "nothing",
              "RDB",
              "AOF everysec",
              "AOF always"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Left to right: weakest to strongest on one box",
            "AOF `always` is the ceiling for a single node",
            "Both mechanisms fork, so neither escapes COW",
            "Both show up in `latest_fork_usec`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pick",
            "When"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Both",
              "production; Redis's own advice"
            ],
            [
              "RDB only",
              "cache-like data, huge set, fast restart"
            ],
            [
              "AOF only",
              "disk cheap, low loss, no file backups"
            ],
            [
              "Neither",
              "pure cache, warmup is cheap"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "AOF-only is rare — you still want RDB backups",
            "RDB is the DR artifact, AOF is the low-RPO log",
            "\"Neither\" assumes a real system of record behind it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "One sentence: which do I run?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Both — `appendonly yes` plus `save` lines",
            "AOF covers the last second, RDB the last week",
            "You pay the fork tax either way"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas & Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "MISCONF Locks Writes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "MISCONF Redis is configured to save RDB snapshots,",
            "but is currently not able to persist on disk.",
            "# usually a full disk or bad `dir` permissions"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Writes are rejected because a BGSAVE failed",
            "Fix the disk, not `stop-writes-on-bgsave-error no`",
            "That flag turns loud failure into silent data loss"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Disk Space Arithmetic"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A BGSAVE writes a full temp copy before renaming",
            "An AOF rewrite writes a full new base too",
            "Each needs room for a second whole dataset",
            "Sizing `dir` at 1x is how you meet MISCONF"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`appendonly yes` in file, no AOF",
              "boots empty"
            ],
            [
              "`CONFIG SET`, no `CONFIG REWRITE`",
              "reverts on restart"
            ],
            [
              "`SAVE` on a big instance",
              "blocks for minutes"
            ],
            [
              "`no-appendfsync-on-rewrite yes`",
              "unmonitored footgun"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SAVE` exists for scripts and shutdown paths, not you",
            "The rewrite window is exactly when durability quietly drops"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Kernel Bites"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "Can't save in background: fork: Cannot allocate memory",
            "# missing vm.overcommit_memory=1, intermittent under load",
            "# THP left on: mystery multi-hundred-ms spikes at save time"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Copying Files Safely",
          "items": [
            "Copying `dump.rdb` mid-BGSAVE is safe — rename saves you",
            "Copying the temp file is not — it is half written",
            "ext4 `data=writeback` is weaker than `data=ordered`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Replica Assumptions"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Snapshots on a primary hurt latency — move them to a replica",
            "But that replica's dataset can lag the primary",
            "A replica does not persist its own view unless configured",
            "Never assume the replica has a usable RDB"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "FLUSHALL Is A Race",
          "text": "It replicates and it lands in the AOF. Recovery means grabbing a pre-incident RDB fast, before a rewrite overwrites the history."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Untested Backups Aren't Backups",
          "items": [
            "Restore into a scratch instance on a schedule",
            "Diff `DBSIZE` against the source",
            "Spot-check a handful of known keys"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Production Playbook & Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Baseline Config",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "appendonly yes",
            "appendfsync everysec",
            "aof-use-rdb-preamble yes",
            "save 900 1",
            "save 300 100"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep `stop-writes-on-bgsave-error yes` — fail loudly",
            "`dir` on a dedicated volume, 2-3x dataset headroom",
            "Owned by the `redis` user, not root"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Host Prep",
          "items": [
            "THP set to `never`",
            "`vm.overcommit_memory=1`",
            "`maxmemory` well below RAM for COW headroom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Monitor These Five"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Metric",
            "Alert when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`rdb_last_bgsave_status`",
              "not `ok`"
            ],
            [
              "`aof_last_bgrewrite_status`",
              "not `ok`"
            ],
            [
              "`aof_last_write_status`",
              "not `ok`"
            ],
            [
              "`latest_fork_usec`",
              "over latency budget"
            ],
            [
              "`rdb_last_save_time`",
              "older than your RPO"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`rdb_changes_since_last_save` is the sixth to watch",
            "It tells you what a crash would cost right now"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Backup Pipeline"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "BGSAVE on replica",
              "LASTSAVE advances",
              "redis-check-rdb",
              "ship offsite, timestamped"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Retention",
          "items": [
            "Hourly for a day",
            "Daily for a month",
            "Enough to undo a logical mistake found late"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Durability Ladder"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "none",
              "RDB",
              "AOF everysec",
              "AOF always",
              "+ WAITAOF"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pay `always` where you must, not globally",
            "`WAITAOF 1 1 <timeout>` on critical writes instead",
            "Redis is a fast tier, never the last copy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Lines To Keep"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mechanism",
            "Shape",
            "Loss"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "RDB",
              "forked binary snapshot",
              "minutes"
            ],
            [
              "AOF",
              "command log + fsync dial",
              "~1s everysec"
            ],
            [
              "Hybrid",
              "RDB base + AOF tail",
              "~1s, fast load"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Handbook",
          "text": "Fork and COW are the shared tax; `write()` vs `fsync()` is the shared distinction. Test your restore before you need it."
        }
      ]
    }
